\begin{itemize}[leftmargin=*, nosep, itemsep=6pt]
    \item \textbf{Data Integrity \& Migration:} We  chose \textbf{PostgreSQL} with \textbf{Flask-Migrate (Alembic)} to enforce strict relational constraints. Resolved a multi-head migration issue to ensure fresh deployments never fail.
    \item \textbf{State Persistence (SET NULL constraint):} Designed the schema so \texttt{FocusSession} records use \texttt{SET NULL} when a milestone is deleted. \textit{Trade-off:} Requires handling nulls in queries, but guarantees students never lose logged study time.
    \item \textbf{Exactly-Once Reminders:} Implemented a unique delivery key (item + offset + day) on the \texttt{Reminder} table. \textit{Trade-off:} Adds slight schema complexity, but prevents duplicate emails if the worker runs multiple times.
    \item \textbf{Security Architecture:} Used \textbf{Fernet} encryption for Canvas tokens and Argon2id for passwords. \textit{Trade-off:} Higher CPU overhead, but mandatory for protecting sensitive third-party API access.
    \item \textbf{Fault Tolerance:} The Canvas sync worker isolates failures per account. One broken token will not stop the rest of the student body from syncing their assignments.
    \item \textbf{Optional AI Integration:} Integrated \textbf{LangGraph} as an optional feature so the core app remains fast and functional without relying on heavy LLM inference for basic planning.
\end{itemize}


